W: Chorus:
W: Fhír a’ Bhàta no hóró eile,
W: Fhír a’ Bhàta no hóró eile,
W: Fhír a’ Bhàta no hóró eile,
W: May joy await thee, where’er thou sailest.
W:
W: 1. Forever haunting the highest hilltops,
W: I scan the ocean, thy sails to see.
W: Wilt come tonight love? Wilt come tomorrow?
W: Wilt ever come love, to comfort me?
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 2. They call you fickle, they call you "false one,"
W: They seek to change me, but all in vain;
W: For thou'rt my dream yet throughout the dark night,
W: And every morning I watch the main.
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 3. There's not a hamlet but well I knew it,
W: Where you go walking or stay awhile,
W: And all its old folk you win with talking,
W: And charm its maidens with song and smile.
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 4. Don't you remember what you did promise:
W: The tartan plaid and the silken gown,
W: The golden ring with your hair and portrait
W: The gown and ring I ne'er will own.
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 5. From passing boatmen I would discover,
W: If they had heard of or seen my lover,
W: I'm never answered; I'm only chided,
W: And told my heart has been sore misguided.
W: (Chorus)
